# The checklist draws a list, reads the real tasks, and keeps what you ticked.
#
# It places a tick box and a row of text against the host's own font, so it
# needs to ask how wide text is.
#
# `save` and `load` are ForgeTerm ADR 0033 and its amendment 0034: the host
# decides what a plugin may write, and this one writes ONE file, under docs/,
# in the project the window is working in. It cannot reach source, `.git`, a
# dotfile, or a second project — those refusals are the host's, not this
# plugin's promise.
#
# `load` is now also how it READS its task list — `docs/visuals/testing.md` —
# rather than drawing a slice compiled into the wasm (ADR 0154, todo74#P3).
# Carried over unchanged from the manifest this plugin had before the move: a
# manifest missing one of these three lines makes the plugin fail to LOAD
# entirely, not fail at the call the missing capability would have answered.
measure-text
save
load
